  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the text_chunk",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'can afford to travel from romania to london still picks your pocket' because the phrase 'picks your pocket' directly addresses the viewer ('you') as the victim of theft. This creates a direct deictic link where the user is positioned as the target of the accusation, making the user feel personally implicated in the scenario described. The projection is onto the text_chunk, which contains the deictic pronoun 'your', thereby anchoring the user's identity to the narrative of being robbed by the elderly woman.",
